# Acrobatic Cheerleader, Survival: "if this creature is tapped" is an intervening "if" (CR 603.4), checked when the second main
# phase begins. It does not attack on turn 3, so it is untapped and the ability does not trigger (nothing on the stack, no counter).
# That leaves its one trigger unused: on turn 5 it attacks, is tapped at the second main phase and gets the flying counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Jet
Acrobatic Cheerleader
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Acrobatic Cheerleader.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Acrobatic Cheerleader.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Acrobatic Cheerleader.Counters.Flying = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Acrobatic Cheerleader > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Acrobatic Cheerleader.Counters.Flying = 1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 18
